  "findings": [
    "Both ranks execute 64 FP16 rowchunk custom ops: 53 receive 512 input rows and expand to 848 separate 32-row FP16 GEMMs; the other 11 receive one row. Another 48 FP16 GEMMs have [256,2560] x [2560,32] shapes outside rowchunk, giving 907 FP16 GEMMs total per rank.",
    "The two most frequent 32-row shapes are [32,2048] x [2048,2560] (400 calls) and [32,2560] x [2560,6144] (384 calls). FP16 mm kernels are the largest directly attributed device operator group on both ranks.",
    "INT4 GEMMs remain substantial: 83 kernels per rank. GDN attention has 24 CPU calls and 168 directly attributed device kernels per rank. These are separate from the FP16 mm device group.",
    "Allreduce kernel time differs sharply by rank: approximately 9.02 ms on rank0 and 21.96 ms on rank1. Collective durations can include synchronization/waiting; this trace does not isolate wire-transfer cost or prove a communication optimization.",
    "The sole full-vocabulary matrix multiplication has one input row: [1,2560] x [2560,124160]. The trace does not support treating the vocabulary projection as a 512-row prefill bottleneck.",
    "A one-token output cap does not remove all speculative work: the captured execution has additional one-row calls with MTP-shaped weights. Treat the profile as the actual configured serving path, not an isolated target-only forward."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Profiler instrumentation and shape recording alter host overhead and scheduling; these timings are diagnostic and must not enter the public prefill-rate table.",
    "One request cannot establish repeatability, control drift, optimization benefit, output quality or decode regression. The parent campaign owns token equality and unprofiled controls.",
    "CPU inclusive time is not GPU execution time. Device kernel sums are not HTTP TTFT, server prefill duration or a causal critical-path decomposition. CPU/GPU execution and tensor-parallel ranks can overlap.",
    "The trace records kernel names and shapes but does not establish exact arithmetic equivalence of alternate GEMM implementations, larger row shapes, batching, graph capture, fusion or allocation lifetime changes.",
    "Directly attributed operator rows omit descendant kernels by design; for example rowchunk has no direct device kernel and its inclusive descendant kernels are reported separately.",
    "Unknown/unattributed device events remain included in device totals; operator summaries are selected groups rather than a partition of all work."
  ],
  "conclusion": {
    "new_small_same_arithmetic_candidate_established": false,
